  "description": "RUDWUL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H58 Dy4 N18 O20. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.900-3.944 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.15-114.76°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(L5)2(μ3-OH)2(Ac)6(NO3)2]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
